# 必考词 Unit12
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit12核心高频词汇

{{hostile}}{/ˈhɒstaɪl/}}{adj. 敌对的；不友好的}}{{The two countries had a hostile relationship for decades.}}

{{household}}{/ˈhaʊshəʊld/}}{n. 家庭；adj. 家用的}}{{Household expenses have increased significantly this year.}}

{{humble}}{/ˈhʌmbl/}}{adj. 谦虚的；卑微的}}{{Despite his success, he remains humble and down-to-earth.}}

{{identical}}{/aɪˈdentɪkl/}}{adj. 完全相同的}}{{The twins wore identical outfits to the party.}}

{{identify}}{/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/}}{v. 识别；确认}}{{The police identified the suspect through security footage.}}

{{identity}}{/aɪˈdentəti/}}{n. 身份；特性}}{{Cultural identity plays an important role in personal development.}}

{{ignorance}}{/ˈɪɡnərəns/}}{n. 无知；愚昧}}{{Ignorance of the law is no excuse for breaking it.}}

{{illustrate}}{/ˈɪləstreɪt/}}{v. 说明；图解}}{{The teacher used a diagram to illustrate the concept.}}

{{image}}{/ˈɪmɪdʒ/}}{n. 形象；图像}}{{The company is trying to improve its public image.}}

{{imagine}}{/ɪˈmædʒɪn/}}{v. 想象；设想}}{{Can you imagine living on another planet?}}

{{imitate}}{/ˈɪmɪteɪt/}}{v. 模仿；仿效}}{{Children often imitate the behavior of their parents.}}

{{immense}}{/ɪˈmens/}}{adj. 巨大的；无限的}}{{The project requires an immense amount of effort.}}

{{immune}}{/ɪˈmjuːn/}}{adj. 免疫的；不受影响的}}{{Vaccines help the body build immunity against diseases.}}

{{impact}}{/ˈɪmpækt/}}{n./v. 影响；冲击}}{{The new policy had a significant impact on the economy.}}

{{implement}}{/ˈɪmplɪment/}}{v. 实施；n. 工具}}{{The government plans to implement the new education policy.}}

{{implication}}{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn/}}{n. 含义；暗示；影响}}{{The findings have important implications for future research.}}

{{imply}}{/ɪmˈplaɪ/}}{v. 暗示；意味着}}{{His silence implied that he disagreed with the decision.}}

{{impose}}{/ɪmˈpəʊz/}}{v. 施加；强制执行}}{{The government imposed strict regulations on pollution.}}

{{impress}}{/ɪmˈpres/}}{v. 给...留下印象}}{{Her presentation impressed everyone at the conference.}}

{{improve}}{/ɪmˈpruːv/}}{v. 改善；提高}}{{Regular practice can improve your language skills.}}

{{incident}}{/ˈɪnsɪdənt/}}{n. 事件；事故}}{{The incident attracted widespread media attention.}}

{{incline}}{/ɪnˈklaɪn/}}{v. 倾斜；倾向}}{{I am inclined to agree with your proposal.}}

{{income}}{/ˈɪnkʌm/}}{n. 收入；所得}}{{The average income has risen steadily over the years.}}

{{incredible}}{/ɪnˈkredəbl/}}{adj. 难以置信的；惊人的}}{{The view from the mountaintop was absolutely incredible.}}

{{independent}}{/ˌɪndɪˈpendənt/}}{adj. 独立的；自主的}}{{She became financially independent after graduation.}}

{{indicate}}{/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/}}{v. 表明；指出}}{{Research indicates that sleep is essential for memory.}}

{{individual}}{/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl/}}{adj. 个人的；n. 个人}}{{Each individual has the right to freedom of expression.}}

{{industry}}{/ˈɪndəstri/}}{n. 工业；行业}}{{The tourism industry contributes greatly to the economy.}}

{{inevitable}}{/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/}}{adj. 不可避免的}}{{Change is inevitable in a rapidly developing world.}}

{{influence}}{/ˈɪnfluəns/}}{n./v. 影响；感化}}{{Teachers have a profound influence on their students' lives.}}

{{inform}}{/ɪnˈfɔːrm/}}{v. 通知；告知}}{{Please inform us of any changes to the schedule.}}

{{inhabit}}{/ɪnˈhæbɪt/}}{v. 居住；栖息}}{{Many species inhabit the tropical rainforest.}}

{{initial}}{/ɪˈnɪʃl/}}{adj. 最初的；n. 首字母}}{{The initial results of the experiment were promising.}}

{{initiate}}{/ɪˈnɪʃieɪt/}}{v. 发起；开始}}{{The company initiated a new training program for employees.}}

{{innocent}}{/ˈɪnəsnt/}}{adj. 无辜的；天真的}}{{The jury declared the defendant innocent.}}

{{innovation}}{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/}}{n. 创新；革新}}{{Innovation is the driving force behind economic growth.}}

{{input}}{/ˈɪnpʊt/}}{n. 输入；投入}}{{Your input on this project would be greatly appreciated.}}

{{inquire}}{/ɪnˈkwaɪər/}}{v. 询问；调查}}{{She inquired about the availability of the room.}}

{{insight}}{/ˈɪnsaɪt/}}{n. 洞察力；见解}}{{The book provides valuable insights into human behavior.}}

{{insist}}{/ɪnˈsɪst/}}{v. 坚持；坚决要求}}{{He insisted on paying for everyone's dinner.}}
